### 19 TAC 89.1055 - Content of the IEP

In addition to the requirements of 34 CFR 300.320, each student's IEP must include:
(1) the projected dates for initiation and duration of services;
(2) the anticipated frequency of services;
(3) the location of services;
(4) a statement of needed transition services for students beginning no later than when the student turns 14;
(5) for students beginning at age 16, a statement of interagency responsibilities or linkages;
(6) the schedule for reevaluation.

### 19 TAC 89.1075 - General Program Requirements and Local District Procedures

(a) Instruction and services for eligible students with disabilities shall be provided by appropriately certified or licensed professionals.
(b) Students with disabilities shall be provided instructional materials at the same time as general education students.
(c) The general education teacher in the ARD committee meeting shall, to the extent appropriate, participate in the development of the student's IEP, including the determination of appropriate positive behavioral interventions and supports, supplementary aids and services, program modifications, and supports for school personnel.

